{\b What Setup changes}\par
Setup installs factor.exe in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\Factor, adds that folder to your PATH, and adds Factor to the Start menu. It needs no administrator rights. Removing Factor in Settings > Apps undoes all three, stops Factor, and removes the login entry the setup wizard adds if you ask it to. Your settings and memory in %USERPROFILE%\\.factor are kept.\par
\par
{\b Privacy}\par
Factor sends your conversations only where you point it: to the language-model providers you configure, to the channels you turn on, and to the sites and services its tools use for your requests. It has no telemetry, and it switches off the telemetry of every engine, library and browser it runs. On its own it contacts GitHub (new releases and the decision model), PyPI, npm and Hugging Face (its components and their models), your package manager (the media player) and OpenRouter (prices), sending none of your data; each of these can be turned off. Details: https://github.com/cyqlelabs/factor#privacy\par
